  "text": "a 1e minus 8 denser, then that is actually just 0. So you can't really represent very big numbers, and you can't represent very small numbers. And the reason is that this exponent is only 5 bits of exponent compared to 8. So if you train with FP16, which people did back in the day, you will get instability. You'll get underflow, you'll get overflow, you'll get NANDs,",
